// show=false -> printable (bare cradle on the wedge). show=true -> preview with
// the board + screen + camera seated in the cradle (used by product()).
module board_cradle_stand(show = false) {
    OW = BM_W + 2*BM_WALL;
    OH = BM_H + 2*BM_WALL;
    lift = OH * sin(BM_TILT);
    difference() {
        union() {
            translate([0, 0, lift]) rotate([BM_TILT, 0, 0])
                if (show) screen_holder(); else board_cradle();
            bm_leg( (OW/2 - BM_WALL/2), OH, lift);
            bm_leg(-(OW/2 - BM_WALL/2), OH, lift);
        }
        // trim to a flat bottom at z = 0
        translate([0, 0, -100]) cube([500, 500, 200], center = true);
    }
}
BM_LIFT = (BM_H + 2*BM_WALL) * sin(BM_TILT);   // how high the wedge raises the cradle

text:
This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.

Summary:
1. Primary Request and Intent:
   This is a continuation session for **VelaPaw** — an on-device-AI multi-pet smart feeder (contest 2026, team contest2026_043_CircuitForge, GitHub login KingMbewe; project at **D:\openVela**, NOT C:). All work this session is **3D CAD in OpenSCAD** on `D:\openVela\contest2026_043_CircuitForge\hardware\velapaw_feeder.scad`. Sequential explicit user intents:
   - (Resumed from prior) "Make sure that the holder is not blocking the GPIO header exit" — COMPLETED.
   - "validate any measurement to make sure and also make sure we have all the parts to be printed" — COMPLETED (found + fixed the missing `stand` part; produced validation report).
   - "yes fix that" — fix the two mechanical findings (chute catch gap/shallow slope; chute+mount not fused to frame) — COMPLETED.
   - "yes" / "open it" — open the model in the OpenSCAD GUI — done multiple times.
   - "does the rotor has a hole where the shaft will be pluged into" — answered YES with a cutaway render.
   - "How does the board cradle make an angle if the 2 pairs of the stand are of the same height?" — explained the wedge-leg geometry with a render.
   - "But the full product doesnt show this stands" — user noticed the product uses the rail mount, not the wedge stand. I asked how to reconcile.
   - **CURRENT (via AskUserQuestion, JUST answered, NOT yet started): "Use the wedge stand in product"** — replace the cantilevered `mount_back` rails with the wedge `board_cradle_stand` sitting on the base plate beside the bowl; camera then looks out/down at 30° (not straight down); print `board_cradle_stand` (one part); rails removed.

   **STANDING CONSTRAINTS THAT MUST PERSIST (verbatim intent from prior context):**
   - **"log no push"**: export AI-coding logs into `D:\openVela\contest2026_043_CircuitForge\logs\KingMbewe\` — **write files ONLY, NEVER git commit/push**.
   - Board-file swaps must preserve the LCD/camera code.
   - Raw `spi_flash` at offset **0x818000 WEDGES the SoC**.
   - **Never enable CONFIG_RTC** (kills the USB console).
   - Console is on USB-Serial/JTAG; UART0 pins (GPIO43/44) can be stolen for GPIO. Stepper IN4 must be GPIO43 (not 44).

2. Key Technical Concepts:
   - **OpenSCAD** parametric CAD; `part` Customizer dropdown variable; `-D 'name="value"'` CLI overrides; `--camera=tx,ty,tz,rotx,roty,rotz,dist` gimbal form (dist=0 renders BLANK); `--projection=ortho`; `--colorscheme=Tomorrow`; F5=preview, F6=full render.
   - **Coordinate frame**: drum axis along +Y, drum spans world Y 0..39 (HOUSING_H=39), center Y=19.5; drum center z=0, outer radius BORE_R+WALL=32, drum bottom/outlet at z=-32; outlet window spans world Y 3..36, X±17 (INLET_W/2=17). Bowl at BOWL_CY=−60 (front/−Y), BOWL_D=130, BOWL_DEP=50; bowl top rim z=−54, near rim at Y=+5, bowl footprint Y−125..+5. STAND_BASE_Z=−104. A-frame supports at SUPP_Y1=−2, SUPP_Y2=41.
   - **Camera aim**: CAM_TILT = atan2(PET_FACE_Y−CAM_MOUNT_Y, CAM_MOUNT_Z−PET_FACE_Z) ≈ −7° (nearly flat, tilts forward toward −Y/pet). CAM_MOUNT_Y=−68, CAM_MOUNT_Z=62. Front layout: CAM_F_Y=−128, CAM_F_Z=34, CAM_F_TILT.
   - **board_cradle_stand wedge**: BM_TILT=30°; each `bm_leg` is a `hull()` between a flat ground bar (z=0) and a tilted+lifted top bar (`rotate([BM_TILT,0,0])` + `lift = OH*sin(BM_TILT)`≈34); whole thing trimmed flat at z=0. Only TWO legs (left/right at ±X), identical because tilt is about X axis (front-to-back). OW=BM_W+2*BM_WALL≈99.9, OH=BM_H+2*BM_WALL≈68.5.
   - **Rotor D-socket**: Ø5.25 (5.0mm shaft +0.25 clearance) intersected with a 3.25mm slab → two flats keying the 28BYJ-48 double-flatted (3mm-across-flats) shaft; depth 8.6mm; blind in the driven (bottom) face. Plus a top stub-axle socket Ø6.3, depth 8.1, for the idle plate's 6mm stub. ~21mm solid hub between them.
   - **STL manifold validation**: exporting each part to STL and checking for warnings/errors + non-zero size = the real "printable" test.
   - **Waveshare ESP32-S3-Touch-LCD-3.5-C** board: 95.11×63.67×14.1mm, corner R7.30, 4 holes 72×48.5mm.

3. Files and Code Sections:
   - **D:\openVela\contest2026_043_CircuitForge\hardware\velapaw_feeder.scad** (the sole file edited):
     - **Line 43 (part dropdown), NOW includes `stand`:**
       `part = "product"; // [product:...,all:...,rotor, housing, plate_stepper, plate_idle, hopper, board_cradle, board_cradle_stand, stand]`
     - **Header comment**: added a `part="stand"` printing note (large; split frame/chute/camera-mount).
     - **mount_back() — REWRITTEN to frame-only + anchor brace** (this is the mount the user just decided to REPLACE with the wedge stand):
       ```scad
       module mount_back() {   // printable camera-mount frame only (no board/electronics)
           RX = 30;   // rail/riser offset from centre (X)
           RW = 14;   // rail/riser width
           color("DimGray")
               for (s = [-1, 1]) {
                   sx = s * RX;
                   translate([sx - RW/2, -95, 12]) cube([RW, 95, 10]);                     // side rail
                   translate([sx - RW/2, -95, 12]) cube([RW, 12, CAM_MOUNT_Z - 12]);       // front riser
                   translate([sx - RW/2, -62, 12]) cube([RW, 12, CAM_MOUNT_Z - 12]);       // mid riser
                   hull() {
                       translate([sx - RW/2, -2, 12]) cube([RW, 8, 6]);                    // on the rail, over support1
                       translate([s * 33 - 5, -2, 34]) cube([10, 8, 10]);                  // onto the solid top bar
                   }
               }
       }
       ```
     - **mount_front() — frame only** (post + foot to base), unchanged logic.
     - **screen_holder_placed() — NEW helper** (places board cradle preview):
       ```scad
       module screen_holder_placed() {
           if (LAYOUT == "front")
               translate([0, CAM_F_Y, CAM_F_Z]) rotate([CAM_F_TILT, 0, 0]) screen_holder();
           else
               translate([0, CAM_MOUNT_Y, CAM_MOUNT_Z]) rotate([CAM_TILT, 0, 0]) screen_holder();
       }
       ```
     - **chute() — REWRITTEN** (catches whole outlet, ~19° slope, legs to base):
       ```scad
       module chute() {
           color("Silver") {
               hull() {
                   translate([-18, 36, -33]) cube([36, 2, 2]);      // back, under the outlet
                   translate([-18, -8, -49]) cube([36, 2, 2]);      // front, launches into the bowl
               }
               for (sx = [-18, 16])
                   hull() {
                       translate([sx, 36, -33]) cube([2, 2, 15]);
                       translate([sx, -8, -49]) cube([2, 2, 15]);
                   }
               translate([-18, 37, -33]) cube([36, 2.5, 6]);        // back lip
               for (sx = [-18, 14])
                   translate([sx, 35, STAND_BASE_Z - 4]) cube([4, 4, -33 - (STAND_BASE_Z - 4)]);  // legs to base
           }
       }
       ```
     - **stand() — structural only** (base + ring + supports + chute + mount FRAME):
       `...stand_support(SUPP_Y1); stand_support(SUPP_Y2); } chute(); if (LAYOUT == "front") mount_front(); else mount_back();`
     - **product() — adds screen_holder_placed():**
       ```scad
       module product() {
           assembly();
           stand();
           screen_holder_placed();
           color("BurlyWood") bowl();
           pet_head_marker();
           camera_sightline();
       }
       ```
     - **Dispatch (bottom):** added `else if (part == "stand") stand();`
     - **board_cradle_stand() (UNCHANGED, the target part for the new task):**
       ```scad
       module bm_leg(ow_x, oh, lift) {
           translate([ow_x, 0, 0]) hull() {
               translate([0, 0, lift]) rotate([BM_TILT, 0, 0]) translate([-BM_WALL/2, -oh/2, 0]) cube([BM_WALL, oh, 0.1]);
               translate([-BM_WALL/2, -oh/2, 0]) cube([BM_WALL, oh, 0.1]);
           }
       }
       module board_cradle_stand() {
           OW = BM_W + 2*BM_WALL; OH = BM_H + 2*BM_WALL; lift = OH * sin(BM_TILT);
           difference() {
               union() {
                   translate([0, 0, lift]) rotate([BM_TILT, 0, 0]) board_cradle();
                   bm_leg( (OW/2 - BM_WALL/2), OH, lift);
                   bm_leg(-(OW/2 - BM_WALL/2), OH, lift);
               }
               translate([0, 0, -100]) cube([500, 500, 200], center = true);
           }
       }
       ```
     - **board_cradle() header slot (from prior session, still at +Y):**
       `translate([-BM_HDR_W/2, BM_HDR_OFF - BM_HDR_D/2, -0.1]) cube([BM_HDR_W, BM_HDR_D, BM_BASE_T + 0.2]);`
     - Key board_cradle params: BM_W=95.11, BM_H=63.67, BM_CORNER=7.30, BM_HOLE_X=36, BM_HOLE_Y=24.25, BM_SCREW_D=2.2 (assumed), BM_STANDOFF=12, BM_BASE_T=3, BM_WALL=2.4, BM_WALL_H=5, BM_CAM_WIN=14 (assumed), BM_HDR_W=40, BM_HDR_D=8, BM_HDR_OFF=22, BM_TILT=30.

4. Errors and fixes:
   - **GPIO header slot blocked by central riser** (opening task): the mirrored slot (+Y) landed over the old single central mount riser. Fixed by rewriting `mount_back` to two side rails at X±30 with a clear central channel. Verified via bottom render.
   - **Stand not printable / not a selectable part**: only existed inside `product()` and bundled preview electronics. Fixed: split mounts to frame-only, moved `screen_holder` preview into `product()` via `screen_holder_placed()`, added `part="stand"`, updated dropdown + header.
   - **Chute missed the back of the outlet + too shallow (~11°)**: chute back was at Y=22 but outlet drops food across Y3..36. Fixed: extended floor back to Y=36, delivery to Y=−8 over the bowl (~19° slope).
   - **Chute + camera mount floating (not fused to frame)**: Fixed by adding chute legs down to the base plate (behind the bowl so they clear it) and a diagonal anchor brace tying each mount rail into the A-frame's solid top bar. Small follow-up: sank chute legs to `STAND_BASE_Z - 4` for solid engagement with the base tray floor (was only 0.5mm).
   - **PowerShell GUI launch warning "Ignoring unknown variable 'board_cradle_stand'"**: `Start-Process -ArgumentList` (array form) stripped the quotes, so OpenSCAD saw `part=board_cradle_stand` (unquoted identifier). Fixed by relaunching with a single-string ArgumentList and escaped quotes: `'-D part=\"board_cradle_stand\" "D:\...\velapaw_feeder.scad"'`. Also offered the Customizer fallback (set part → board_cradle_stand, F5).

5. Problem Solving:
   - Verified all 7 core parts (rotor, housing, plate_stepper, plate_idle, hopper, board_cradle, board_cradle_stand) export as clean non-zero manifold STLs; added and verified `stand` (226KB).
   - Delivered a measurement validation report: confirmed rotor/bore clearance, D-shaft socket, stepper flange (35mm holes, 8mm offset — matches 28BYJ-48), idle stub, hopper saddle, board cradle hole pattern; flagged 3 assumed values (BM_SCREW_D=2.2, BM_CAM_WIN=14, board outline/holes) to verify before printing.
   - Explained rotor shaft socket (D-keyed, blind, press-fit) with a cutaway; noted orientation-matters and clearance-tuning caveats.
   - Explained the wedge-leg tilt mechanism.
   - Surfaced the redundancy between the appliance rail-mount and the standalone wedge stand; presented 3 options via AskUserQuestion.

6. All user messages:
   - "Its looking alright, one last thing validate any measurement to make sure and also make sure we have all the parts to be printed"
   - "yes fix that"
   - "yes"
   - "One thing does the rotor has a hole where the shaft will be pluged into"
   - "yes"
   - "How does the board cradle make an angle if the 2 pairs of the stand are of the same height?"
   - "open it"
   - "WARNING: Ignoring unknown variable 'board_cradle_stand' in file velapaw_feeder.scad, line 625"
   - [screenshot] "the board has a stand like in the image"
   - [screenshot of product] "But the full product doesnt show this stands per attached image"
   - (AskUserQuestion answer) "Use the wedge stand in product"
   - (final) CRITICAL instruction to produce this summary with text only.

7. Pending Tasks:
   - **CURRENT (just decided, NOT started): "Use the wedge stand in product"** — Modify the model so the full `product`/`stand` mounts the board on the wedge `board_cradle_stand` sitting on the base plate beside the bowl, REMOVE the `mount_back` cantilevered rails, and re-aim the camera to look out/down at ~30° at the pet (rather than straight down over the bowl). The BOM for the appliance would then use `board_cradle_stand` (one part) instead of `board_cradle` + rail mount.
   - (Standing) Confirm the real Waveshare board's assumed values (BM_SCREW_D, BM_CAM_WIN, outline/holes) before printing.
   - (Standing) Re-export logs (files only, NO push) if requested.

8. Current Work:
   Immediately before this summary, I asked the user (via AskUserQuestion) how the board should mount in the full product, after they observed "But the full product doesnt show this stands per attached image." I explained the product currently uses the DimGray `mount_back` rails (camera over the bowl looking straight down) while `board_cradle_stand` is a separate freestanding desk part with 30° wedge legs, and that they can't both be right for one build. The user selected **"Use the wedge stand in product"**: "Replace the cantilevered rails with the wedge stand sitting on the base plate beside the bowl. More rigid, reuses one part — but the camera then looks out/down at 30°, not straight down over the bowl." (preview: "product = wedge stand on base plate / camera -> 30 deg out/down at pet / print: board_cradle_stand (one part) / rails removed"). I have NOT yet made any edit for this — no code changes started for this task.

9. Optional Next Step:
   Implement the user's chosen option "Use the wedge stand in product": edit `velapaw_feeder.scad` so the `stand()`/`product()` (back layout) places `board_cradle_stand()` on the base plate beside/behind the bowl instead of calling `mount_back()` + `screen_holder_placed()` on the rails. This means: (a) position the wedge stand at a sensible spot on the base plate (e.g., on the −Y front platform or beside the bowl) so the tilted board's camera faces the pet at ~30°; (b) remove/disable the `mount_back` rails in the back layout; (c) update the preview aids (camera_sightline / pet_head_marker) and CAM_ACT/PET_ACT so the red sightline still lands on the pet-head marker from the new 30° position; (d) render `part="product"` and `part="stand"` to verify the board sits on its wedge legs, the camera aim lands on the pet, and nothing collides; (e) re-export the STL to confirm it stays manifold. Verbatim task confirmation — user's AskUserQuestion answer: **"Use the wedge stand in product"** with description "Replace the cantilevered rails with the wedge stand sitting on the base plate beside the bowl... the camera then looks out/down at 30°, not straight down over the bowl." Before finalizing camera-aim numbers, confirm the intended stand placement location if it is ambiguous (front platform vs. beside the bowl), since that changes the geometry.

