text:
This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.

Summary:
1. **Primary Request and Intent:**

   This is a continuation session for **VelaPaw** — an on-device-AI multi-pet smart feeder (contest 2026, team contest2026_043_CircuitForge, GitHub login KingMbewe; project at **D:\openVela**, NOT C:). All work this session is **3D CAD in OpenSCAD** on `D:\openVela\contest2026_043_CircuitForge\hardware\velapaw_feeder.scad`.

   Sequential user intents this session:
   - **(Inherited, COMPLETED)** "Use the wedge stand in product" — replace the cantilevered `mount_back` rails with the wedge `board_cradle_stand`, print `board_cradle_stand` as one part, rails removed.
   - **"yes"** — open the model in the OpenSCAD GUI. DONE (PID 20044).
   - **(COMPLETED)** "Its too close to the drum so move it a lit to the front and also move the same measurement the board on the bowl to the front also" — move the board forward away from the drum, and move the bowl forward by the same measurement.
   - **CURRENT / NOT STARTED:** "Move it again so that the screen a user can see without the funnel blocking" — clarified by the user when rejecting a tool call: **"Yes do that because there has to be a good space betwe the screen and the funnel"**. So: reposition so the user can see the screen unobstructed, AND there is a good physical SPACE/gap between the screen and the funnel.

   **STANDING CONSTRAINTS THAT MUST PERSIST (verbatim intent from prior context):**
   - **"log no push"**: export AI-coding logs into `D:\openVela\contest2026_043_CircuitForge\logs\KingMbewe\` — **write files ONLY, NEVER git commit/push**.
   - Board-file swaps must preserve the LCD/camera code.
   - Raw `spi_flash` at offset **0x818000 WEDGES the SoC**.
   - **Never enable CONFIG_RTC** (kills the USB console).
   - Console is on USB-Serial/JTAG; UART0 pins (GPIO43/44) can be stolen for GPIO. Stepper IN4 must be GPIO43 (not 44).

2. **Key Technical Concepts:**
   - **OpenSCAD** parametric CAD; `part` Customizer dropdown; CLI `-D` overrides; `--camera=tx,ty,tz,rotx,roty,rotz,dist` gimbal; `--projection` accepts only **`o`** or **`p`** (NOT `ortho`/`persp` — those error); `--colorscheme=Tomorrow`; F5 preview / F6 full render.
   - **OpenSCAD variable hoisting**: top-level variable assignments are order-independent, so `BM_LIFT` defined late in the file can be referenced by `CAM_ACT` earlier.
   - **CGAL manifold validation**: export STL and check `Simple: yes` + `Volumes: 2` (= one connected solid; 3+ = disconnected pieces) + zero WARNING/ERROR.
   - **CGAL intersection collision testing**: a temporary `part` dispatch branch doing `intersection() { A(); B(); }`; empty result prints "Current top level object is empty" and writes no file. Non-empty = real interference. Bounding box of the sliver can be extracted by regex-parsing the ASCII STL `vertex` lines.
   - **Coordinate frame**: drum axis along +Y, drum spans world Y 0..39, drum centre z=0, outer radius 32 (top z+32), outlet window Y 3..36 at z−32. `STAND_BASE_Z = -(BOWL_DEP + DROP_GAP + 32) = -104`. A-frame supports at SUPP_Y1=−2, SUPP_Y2=41, SUPP_W=84 (X±42). Base plate X±82.
   - **Wedge geometry**: `BM_TILT=30`; `rotate([30,0,0])` maps camera axis (0,0,−1)→(0,+0.5,−0.866); after `rotate([0,0,180])` → **(0,−0.5,−0.866)** = camera points −Y (bowl) and down. Screen normal → **(0,+0.5,+0.866)** = up-and-back toward owner. `OH = BM_H+2*BM_WALL = 68.47`; `BM_LIFT = OH*sin(30) = 34.2`; `OW = 99.9`; wedge feet at X ±48.8.
   - **THE KEY CONSTRAINT (drove two redesigns)**: the wedge tilt is fixed at 30°, so the camera can only lie on ONE line back up the sight ray. Raising it also drags it BACKWARD (into the drum/hopper); lowering it drags it FORWARD. Hence the mount is low + forward.
   - **Same-delta shift trick**: shifting wedge + bowl + pet by the SAME delta leaves the camera→pet vector unchanged, so the aim stays exact and `PED_TOP` needs no re-solving.
   - **Screen/camera opposite-face conflict** (the current open problem): screen and camera are on opposite faces of the Waveshare board, so aiming the camera down-forward at the pet NECESSARILY points the screen up-and-back toward the funnel. The original rail mount had `CAM_TILT ≈ −7°` (nearly flat) so the screen faced nearly straight up and was readable from anywhere; the 30° wedge tilt is what buried it behind the funnel.
   - **Waveshare ESP32-S3-Touch-LCD-3.5-C**: 95.11×63.67×14.1mm, corner R7.30, holes 72×48.5mm.

3. **Files and Code Sections:**

   **`D:\openVela\contest2026_043_CircuitForge\hardware\velapaw_feeder.scad`** (the sole file edited all session)

   - **Header print notes (lines ~31-42)** — updated to document the new BOM:
     ```
     //   part="board_cradle"- flat, posts up. No supports. Holds the ESP32-S3 board
     //                        screen-UP with the camera looking DOWN at the bowl.
     //   part="board_cradle_stand" - the board_cradle riding a 30-degree wedge, flat
     //                        feet down. No supports. THIS is the board mount the
     //                        finished appliance uses (it drops onto the stand's
     //                        pedestal); also works as a stand-alone desk stand.
     //   part="stand"       - the structural A-frame + bowl base + chute + the wedge
     //                        PEDESTAL (NO electronics). Large: print base-down; on a
     //                        smaller bed split it (frame / chute / pedestal are the
     //                        natural sub-pieces -- they are separate solids). Pair it
     //                        with a printed board_cradle_stand to complete the build.
     ```

