text:
This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.

Summary:
1. **Primary Request and Intent:**

   Continuation of **VelaPaw** — an on-device-AI multi-pet smart feeder (contest 2026, team contest2026_043_CircuitForge, GitHub login KingMbewe). Project lives at **D:\openVela** (NOT C:). All work this session is 3D CAD in OpenSCAD on the single file `D:\openVela\contest2026_043_CircuitForge\hardware\velapaw_feeder.scad`.

   The session opened by completing a carried-over visual check (`product_iso.png`) and reporting the finished Waveshare board-dimension verification + corner-clamp retention work.

   The user then made four requests:
   - **"BM_CLAMP = 14 ... this is correct and can you explain on the other one"** — confirm BM_CLAMP on the physical board, and explain the remaining open item (the stand exceeding the print bed).
   - **"fix both"** — implement both halves of the bed fix: cut the base plate, and un-fuse the three towers into separate printable parts.
   - **"log no push"** — export the session's AI-coding log into the team repo, files only.
   - **"I bealive right now everything is correct right every part is printable"** — a request to confirm that every part is printable.

   **STANDING CONSTRAINTS THAT MUST PERSIST (verbatim intent):**
   - **"log no push"**: export AI-coding logs into `D:\openVela\contest2026_043_CircuitForge\logs\KingMbewe\` — **write files ONLY, NEVER git commit/push**.
   - Board-file swaps must preserve the LCD/camera code.
   - Raw `spi_flash` at offset **0x818000 WEDGES the SoC**.
   - **Never enable CONFIG_RTC** (kills the USB console).
   - Console is on USB-Serial/JTAG; UART0 pins (GPIO43/44) can be stolen for GPIO. Stepper IN4 must be GPIO43 (not 44).

2. **Key Technical Concepts:**
   - **OpenSCAD** parametric CAD; `part` Customizer dropdown; CLI `-D` overrides; `--camera=eyex,eyey,eyez,cx,cy,cz`; `--colorscheme=Tomorrow`.
   - **`include <>` vs `use <>`**: `include` splices in top-level geometry AND globals (so `-D part="none"` still rendered ~96×96×143 of stray geometry); `use` imports modules/functions only — modules still see their own file's globals, but the *calling* file does not, so `SUPP_Y1` etc. evaluate to `undef` in probe scripts.
   - **CGAL validation**: `Simple: yes` + `Volumes: N` where N−1 = connected solids. **CGAL merges coincident-face unions into ONE volume** — this is what let a "separate" tower export fused to the plate.
   - **What CGAL will NOT catch**: two solids that volumetrically overlap in a union just merge — interference is invisible to `Simple:`/`Volumes:`. Must be found with explicit `intersection()` probes.
   - **Connected-component counting** (`comps.py`): vertex-weld an STL, build a vertex adjacency graph, flood-fill. Catches "these two pieces are actually one solid" that bbox and CGAL flags miss.
   - **Independent mesh audit** (`audit.py`): every undirected edge must appear exactly twice; also reports bbox and bed fit. Globs `a_*.stl`, so files must be prefixed.
   - **Bed-fit geometry**: a 164 × 268 rectangle rotated 45° needs a 305mm square envelope; standing it on edge puts 268 into Z (> 250). Neither saves it.
   - **Print-orientation vs assembly-orientation**: all parts are modelled in assembly coordinates; the measured bboxes are assembly-frame, not the orientation they'd actually be sliced in.
   - **Countersunk vs socket-cap in thin plate**: a ⌀6 counterbore 3mm deep in a 5mm floor leaves 2mm; a 90° countersink sinks 1.5mm and leaves 3.5mm.
   - **PowerShell `-Filter`** has no character-class support; **PowerShell strips quotes** from `-D "part=`"x`""` passed to native exes (use Bash).
   - **Contest log tool** crashes on a cp1252 console printing its ✅ prefix — needs `PYTHONIOENCODING=utf-8`.

3. **Files and Code Sections:**

   **`D:\openVela\contest2026_043_CircuitForge\hardware\velapaw_feeder.scad`** — the sole file edited.

   - **BM_CLAMP confirmation (~line 422) — EDITED:**
     ```scad
     // CONFIRMED ON THE PHYSICAL BOARD (2026-07-24): the BM_CLAMP reach along each
     // edge really is empty. This was the one value inferred from the drawing rather
     // than measured on the part; it now checks out, so the corner scheme stands.
     ```

   - **New `SPLIT FOR PRINTING` section (inserted before `stand_support`) — ADDED.** Header comment records the measured sub-assembly bboxes and the reasoning:
     ```scad
     // stand() as a single solid measures 164 x 268 x 172 against a 220 x 220 x 250
     // bed. Rotation does not save it: a 164 x 268 rectangle turned 45deg needs a
     // 305mm square envelope, and standing it on edge puts the 268 into Z, over the
     // 250 height. So it has to be cut.
     //     base plate      164 x 268 x  11    <-- the ONLY one that does not fit
     //     A-frames (x2)    90 x  51 x 167        fits
     //     pedestal        108 x  80 x 102        fits
     //     chute            36 x 109 x  96.5      fits
     ```
     Constants:
     ```scad
     BASE_Y0      = BOWL_CY - 68 - BASE_FRONT_EXT;  // plate front edge (-208)
     BASE_Y1      = 60;                             // plate back edge
     BASE_SEAM_Y  = -32;    // the cut. front tile 176mm long, back tile 92mm
     SPLICE_X     = 50;     // splice boss offset from centre (X)
     SPLICE_W     = 24;     // splice boss width  (X)
     SPLICE_L     = 15;     // splice boss reach EACH SIDE of the seam (Y)
     SPLICE_H     = 10;     // 10 not 6 (rim height) so the bolt has 2.5mm under
                            // it and 5mm over it
     SPLICE_Z     = STAND_BASE_Z + SPLICE_H/2;      // bolt axis
     // Bolt: M3 x 22 socket cap -- 4mm of head in the counterbore, 11mm of clearance
     // through the rest of the front boss, 11mm of thread into the back boss's 13mm
     // pilot. Do not go to 25: 11 + 14 would bottom out in that pilot.
     FOOT_T       = 8;      // flange thickness. Deep enough for 7mm of M3 thread.
     FOOT_FIT     = 0.3;    // per-side clearance of the plate's relief pocket
     FOOT_SCREW   = 3.4;    // M3 clearance through the plate
     FOOT_PILOT   = 2.5;    // M3 self-tap pilot in the flange
     FOOT_CSK     = 6.4;    // 90deg countersink major dia under the plate
     ```
     The seam-choice comment (critical rationale):
     ```scad
     // BASE_SEAM_Y = -32 is not arbitrary. ... the constraint is the SPLICE BOSSES
     // (which reach 15mm FORWARD of the seam), not the cut line itself:
     //     bowl locating ring   rearmost point Y = -51   ->  4mm clear of the boss
     //     pedestal foot flange rear edge      Y = -50   ->  3mm clear of the boss
     //     front A-frame flange front edge     Y = -15   ->  2mm clear of the boss
     ```
     Per-tower foot list (after the rework):
     ```scad
     SUPP_FOOT_L  = 16;     // A-frame pad depth (Y); the bar itself is 8
     SUPP_FOOT_X  = 34;     // A-frame screw spread from centre (X)
     CHUTE_LEG_Y  = 17;     // chute leg front edge
     CHUTE_LEG_L  = 8;      // chute leg depth (Y)
     FOOT_SUP = [ for (yc = [SUPP_Y1, SUPP_Y2]) [0, yc, SUPP_W, SUPP_FOOT_L, SUPP_FOOT_X, 0] ];
     FOOT_CHU = [ for (sx = [-16, 16]) [sx, CHUTE_LEG_Y + CHUTE_LEG_L/2, 14, 16, 0, 5] ];
     FOOT_PED = (LAYOUT == "front") ? [] : [ for (sx = [-48, 48]) [sx, -63, 14, 26, 0, 9] ];
     FEET_ALL = concat(FOOT_SUP, FOOT_CHU, FOOT_PED);
     ```
     with the documented Y ranges: `ped pad -76..-50 | splice bosses -47..-17 | front pad -10..6 | chute pad 13..29 | back pad 33..49. Smallest gap 4mm.`

     Modules:
     ```scad
     module tower_foot(f) {
         difference() {
             translate([f[0] - f[2]/2, f[1] - f[3]/2, STAND_BASE_Z]) cube([f[2], f[3], FOOT_T]);
             for (s = [-1, 1])
                 translate([f[0] + s*f[4], f[1] + s*f[5], STAND_BASE_Z - 0.1])
                     cylinder(d = FOOT_PILOT, h = FOOT_T - 1, $fn = 24);
         }
     }
     module foot_pocket(f) {
         translate([f[0] - f[2]/2 - FOOT_FIT, f[1] - f[3]/2 - FOOT_FIT, STAND_BASE_Z - 0.01])
             cube([f[2] + 2*FOOT_FIT, f[3] + 2*FOOT_FIT, 12]);
     }
     module foot_holes(f) {
         for (s = [-1, 1])
             translate([f[0] + s*f[4], f[1] + s*f[5], 0]) {
                 translate([0, 0, STAND_BASE_Z - STAND_BASE_T - 1])
                     cylinder(d = FOOT_SCREW, h = STAND_BASE_T + 4, $fn = 24);
                 translate([0, 0, STAND_BASE_Z - STAND_BASE_T - 0.01])
                     cylinder(d1 = FOOT_CSK, d2 = FOOT_SCREW,
                              h = (FOOT_CSK - FOOT_SCREW) / 2, $fn = 24);
             }
     }
     module y_cyl(x, z, y0, y1, d) {
         translate([x, y0, z]) rotate([-90, 0, 0]) cylinder(d = d, h = y1 - y0, $fn = 24);
     }
     module splice_boss(front) {
         for (s = [-1, 1])
             translate([s * SPLICE_X - SPLICE_W/2,
                        front ? BASE_SEAM_Y - SPLICE_L : BASE_SEAM_Y, STAND_BASE_Z])
                 cube([SPLICE_W, SPLICE_L, SPLICE_H]);
     }
     module splice_bolt_voids() {
         for (s = [-1, 1]) {
             y_cyl(s*SPLICE_X, SPLICE_Z, BASE_SEAM_Y - SPLICE_L - 0.1,
                   BASE_SEAM_Y - SPLICE_L + 4, 6.5);                      // cap head
             y_cyl(s*SPLICE_X, SPLICE_Z, BASE_SEAM_Y - SPLICE_L + 3.9,
                   BASE_SEAM_Y + 0.1, FOOT_SCREW);                        // clearance
             y_cyl(s*SPLICE_X, SPLICE_Z, BASE_SEAM_Y - 0.1,
                   BASE_SEAM_Y + SPLICE_L - 2, FOOT_PILOT);               // pilot
         }
     }
     module base_plate_solid() {
         difference() {
             union() {
                 difference() {
                     translate([-82, BASE_Y0, STAND_BASE_Z - STAND_BASE_T])
                         cube([164, BASE_Y1 - BASE_Y0, STAND_BASE_T + 6]);
                     // tray pocket. Cut at exactly STAND_BASE_Z (it used to start
                     // 0.5mm higher, ... a 0.5mm rock once the towers bolt on).
                     translate([-76, BASE_Y0 + 6, STAND_BASE_Z])
                         cube([152, (BASE_Y1 - 6) - (BASE_Y0 + 6), 10]);
                 }
                 translate([0, BOWL_CY, STAND_BASE_Z])       // bowl locating ring
                     difference() {
                         cylinder(d = BOWL_D + 12, h = 5, $fn = 96);
                         translate([0, 0, -0.1]) cylinder(d = BOWL_D + 2, h = 6, $fn = 96);
                     }
                 splice_boss(true);
                 splice_boss(false);
             }
             for (p = FEET_ALL) { foot_pocket(p); foot_holes(p); }
             splice_bolt_voids();
         }
     }
     module base_half(front) {
         intersection() {
             base_plate_solid();
             translate([-100, front ? BASE_Y0 - 10 : BASE_SEAM_Y,
                        STAND_BASE_Z - STAND_BASE_T - 10])
                 cube([200, front ? BASE_SEAM_Y - (BASE_Y0 - 10)
                                  : (BASE_Y1 + 10) - BASE_SEAM_Y, 40]);
         }
     }
     module base_front() { base_half(true);  }   // 164 x 176 x 15, bowl end
     module base_back()  { base_half(false); }   // 164 x  92 x 15, column end
     ```

   - **`stand_support(yc)` — EDITED** (first line added; note it is ONE foot spanning the whole bar):
     ```scad
     module stand_support(yc) {
         tower_foot([0, yc, SUPP_W, SUPP_FOOT_L, SUPP_FOOT_X, 0]);
         translate([0, yc + SAD_T / 2, 0]) rotate([90, 0, 0]) linear_extrude(SAD_T) ...
     ```

   - **`chute_uz()` — NEW FUNCTION** (added after `CHUTE_RB`):
     ```scad
     function chute_uz(y) = CHUTE_BZ + (36 - y) / (36 - CHUTE_FY) * (CHUTE_FZ - CHUTE_BZ);
     ```

   - **`chute()` legs — REPLACED:**
     ```scad
     for (sx = [-18, 14])
         hull() {
             translate([sx, CHUTE_LEG_Y, STAND_BASE_Z]) cube([4, CHUTE_LEG_L, 1]);
             translate([sx, CHUTE_LEG_Y, chute_uz(CHUTE_LEG_Y) - 1]) cube([4, 0.5, 1.5]);
             translate([sx, CHUTE_LEG_Y + CHUTE_LEG_L - 0.5,
                        chute_uz(CHUTE_LEG_Y + CHUTE_LEG_L) - 1]) cube([4, 0.5, 1.5]);
         }
     for (f = FOOT_CHU) tower_foot(f);
     ```

   - **`mount_back()` — EDITED**: added `tower_foot([px, (PY0 + PY1) / 2, 14, 26, 0, 9]);` inside the post loop, plus the tie bar:
     ```scad
     color("DimGray")
         translate([-(PX + PW/2), -66, STAND_BASE_Z + 7])
             cube([2*(PX + PW/2), 12, 10]);
     ```
     with a long comment tabulating the bowl cone's rear edge by height (`z=-115 -> Y=-73.7`, `z=-105 -> Y=-69.0`, `z=-97 -> Y=-65.9`, `z=-90 -> Y=-63.6`) and recording the −97 mistake.

   - **`stand()` — REWRITTEN as preview-only:**
     ```scad
     module stand() {
         color("Tan")       base_front();
         color("BurlyWood") base_back();
         color("Tan") { stand_support(SUPP_Y1); stand_support(SUPP_Y2); }
         chute();
         if (LAYOUT == "front") mount_front(); else mount_back();
     }
     ```

   - **Part dropdown (line 52) — EDITED:** added `stand:assembled stand preview (do NOT print), base_front, base_back, support:print TWO, chute, pedestal`.

   - **if-chain — EDITED:**
     ```scad
     else if (part == "stand")        stand();       // preview only -- 268mm, will not fit
     // The stand, split for the bed. base_front + base_back bolt together at
     // BASE_SEAM_Y with 2x M3x22 socket cap. support/chute/pedestal then bolt DOWN
     // through the plate with 2x M3x12 countersunk per foot: 6 feet ... = 12 screws.
     // Assembly order: join the two tiles first, then drop the towers on ...
     else if (part == "base_front")   base_front();
     else if (part == "base_back")    base_back();
     else if (part == "support")      stand_support(0);   // print TWO of these
     else if (part == "chute")        chute();
